di Financial Services. All calculation outputs are estimates for educational planning purposes only.</p>\n\n<h2>How to Use the Audi Finance Calculator</h2>\n<p>Calculating your prospective monthly payment with the Audi Finance Calculator is simple, fast, and user-friendly. Follow these numbered steps to model your luxury vehicle loan scenario accurately:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Enter total Vehicle Price:</strong> Input the negotiated selling price of the Audi model, including optional equipment packages, destination fees, and estimated state or provincial sales taxes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Input Down Payment Cash:</strong> Enter the upfront cash down payment you intend to pay. Higher down payments lower your overall borrowing costs significantly.</li>\n  <li><strong>Subtract Net Trade-In Equity:</strong> Enter the appraised value of your current trade-in vehicle minus any existing loan balance owed to your current lender.</li>\n  <li><strong>Enter Annual Interest Rate (APR %):</strong> Input the annual interest rate quoted by your bank, credit union, or captive luxury lender based on your credit profile.</li>\n  <li><strong>Choose Loan Duration (Months):</strong> Select your preferred repayment window, typically ranging from 36 to 72 months for auto loans.</li>\n  <li><strong>Analyze Results & Amortization:</strong> Instantly view your calculated monthly payment, overall interest expense, and detailed payment breakdown schedule table.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Formula and Worked Example</h2>\n<p>Monthly auto loan repayments are computed using standard fixed-rate amortization time-value-of-money mathematics:</p>\n<div class=\"formula-card\">\n  PMT = P * [ r(1 + r)^n ] / [ (1 + r)^n - 1 ]\n</div>\n<p>Where <strong>P</strong> represents net principal financed (Vehicle Price minus Down Payment and Trade-In Allowance), <strong>r</strong> represents the monthly periodic interest rate (Annual APR / 12), and <strong>n</strong> represents total loan payment months.</p>\n<p>To illus