ow to Use the Ford Finance Calculator</h2>\n<p>Estimating your monthly payment with our Ford calculator is quick and straightforward. Follow these numbered steps to model your vehicle loan scenario accurately:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Enter Vehicle Selling Price:</strong> Input the agreed vehicle purchase price, including factory options, destination fees, and estimated state or provincial sales taxes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Input Cash Down Payment:</strong> Enter the upfront cash down payment you plan to provide at signing to reduce the principal balance financed.</li>\n  <li><strong>Add Net Trade-In Equity:</strong> Enter your trade-in vehicle allowance minus any remaining loan balance owed to your existing lender.</li>\n  <li><strong>Specify Interest Rate (APR %):</strong> Input the annual percentage rate quoted by your bank, credit union, or lender based on your credit score profile.</li>\n  <li><strong>Select Repayment Window (Months):</strong> Choose your desired loan duration, typically ranging from 36 to 84 months.</li>\n  <li><strong>Review Monthly Payment & Interest:</strong> Instantly view your calculated monthly payment, total interest cost, and payment amortization schedule table.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Formula and Worked Example</h2>\n<p>Fixed-rate auto loan monthly payments are calculated using standard amortization mathematics:</p>\n<div class=\"formula-card\">\n  PMT = P * [ r(1 + r)^n ] / [ (1 + r)^n - 1 ]\n</div>\n<p>Where <strong>P</strong> represents net principal financed (Vehicle Price minus Down Payment and Trade-In Allowance), <strong>r</strong> represents the monthly periodic interest rate (Annual APR / 12), and <strong>n</strong> represents total monthly payment periods.</p>\n<p>For example, consider a buyer purchasing a new Ford F-150 with a negotiated price of $48,000. The buyer provides a $6,000 cash down payment and receives $2,000 in net trade-in allowance, resulting in a net loan principal (P) of $40,000. The lender quotes an annual interest rate (APR) of 6.49% over a 60-month loan term. The monthly interest rate r equals 0.0649 / 12 = 0.00540833.</p>\n<p>Plugging these numbers into the formula yields a monthly payment of $782.52. Over 60 months, total payments equal $46,951.20, comprising $40,000 in principal balance and $6,951.20 in total compound interest costs. The table below displays this financial summary:</p>\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0;\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"background-color: var(--bg-subtle);\">\n      <th style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: left;\">Loan Parameter</th>\n      <th style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">Financial Value</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Ford Vehicle Selling Price</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">$48,000.00</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Cash Down Payment</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">$6,000.00</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Net Trade-In Credit</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">$2,000.00</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Net Principal Financed (P)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">$40,000.00</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Annual Interest Rate (APR)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">6.49%</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Loan Duration (n)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">60 Months</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; font-weight: bold;\">Monthly Payment (PMT)</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right; font-weight: bold; color: var(--accent-primary);\">$782.52</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Total Interest Cost</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: right;\">$6,951.20</td></tr>\n    <tr><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; font-weight: bold;\">Total Vehicle Investment</td><td style=\"padding: 0.5rem; text-align: